------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web CarAnimation module is a set of PURE presentational primitives (hero / loading illustrations). Each
mark's inputs are plain props (size, level, className) + one display-boundary hook (useMotionPreference());
it draws an SVG and, when motion is allowed, plays an entry + looping animation. There is NO fetch, NO React-
Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading / error / stale / offline branch (these marks ARE the loading
/ hero affordances other surfaces show; there is nothing for them to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from).
Reproducing those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this surface
reproduces only the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the sibling presentational primitives
Spinner (0140), Accordion (0203), StaggerItem (0194), Delta (0081), and MetricCard (0095) used. The REAL
branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • CarAnimation : the staggered entry (body stroke draw-in web pathLength; windshield/rear-window opacity
                   fades; 4 wheels spring-pop with staggered delays; ground shadow scaleX stretch) + the
                   forever head/tail-light opacity pulses; reduced -> the static resting silhouette.
  • ChargingBolt : rise+fade entry (opacity 0→1, y -4→0) + forever fill-opacity pulse [0.1,0.3,0.1]; reduced
                   -> static bolt at fillOpacity 0.2.
  • BatteryFill  : container fade + fill cell grows left→right to 38*clamp(level)/100 in the band color
                   (>=60 good / >=30 warn / else danger, web COLOR.GOOD/WARN/BAD = #10b981/#f59e0b/#ef4444);
                   reduced -> the resting fill, no grow.
  • WheelSpin    : forever 2s linear spoke rotation; reduced -> frozen spokes.
Data source  : useMotionPreference -> CarAnimationMotionPreference.resolve (1:1 port; the live reduce flag
               binds via \.accessibilityReduceMotion, the native peer of useReducedMotion()).
Shared comps : none (the web source uses none).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : the three web aria-label literals (carAnimation.tesla/charging/loading) mirrored through the
               P1/S10 facade with the exact fallback copy; the master Localizable.xcstrings already carries
               translation.carAnimation.{tesla,charging,loading}. The battery gauge has no role/aria in the
               source, so it owns no key.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "CarAnimation" (P1/S11) per mount.
a11y         : reduce-motion honored (the core behaviour, tested across all 4 marks); the 3 labeled marks are
               single image elements with the localized role="img" label (web aria-label) + .isImage trait;
               the battery gauge is decorative (VoiceOver-hidden, faithful to the web's no-role/no-aria SVG —
               a host label owns the readout, as on the web); the inner shapes are decorative; Dynamic Type
               via tokens; no interactive elements (vacuous for "label on every interactive element").
tokens (P1/S9): --theme-primary→accent; --surface-1/2/3→bg/surface/surfaceGlass (elevation order); --text-
               muted→textMuted; taillight #ef4444→statusDanger; battery bands→statusSuccess/Warning/Danger
               (same hex as web COLOR). No raw hex, no Tailwind ports; light/dark/high-contrast safe.

